[7.34041, "o", "{\r\n  \"name\": \"pocketwise-api\",\r\n  \"version\": \"0.31.0\",\r\n  \"private\": true,\r\n  \"type\": \"module\",\r\n  \"engines\": { \"node\": \">=22.6\" },\r\n  \"scripts\": {\r\n    \"start\": \"node --experimental-strip-types --no-warnings src/server.ts\",\r\n    \"test\": \"node --experimental-strip-types --no-warnings --test\"\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n"]
[7.342552, "o", "# Pocketwise API: operations\r\n\r\nTypeScript on Node 22, run with type stripping (no build step):\r\n\r\n```\r\nnode src/server.ts                                   # listen on $PORT\r\nnode src/server.ts replay samples/<file>.json --now 2026-11-16T10:00:00Z\r\nnpm test\r\n```\r\n\r\n`replay` pushes one captured request through the router, which is how we debug webhook\r\ndeliveries. Everything under `samples/` is a capture from the providers' sandboxes.\r\n\r\n## State\r\n\r\nCustomers live in `$APP_DATA/customers.json` (default `data/`). `kyc_status` moves\r\n`pending_kyc -> manual_review | verified | rejected`; `manual_review -> verified | rejected`\r\n(see `src/customers.ts`). A customer cannot add money or send payments until `verified`.\r\n`processed_events` holds the last 50 provider event ids, so a redelivered webhook is a no-op.\r\n\r\n## Webhooks\r\n\r\n| Route | Provider | Secret (`config/secrets.json`) | Header |\r\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\r\n| `POST /webhooks/paylark` | Paylark (card top-ups) | `paylark` | `Paylark-Signature` |\r\n\r\nBoth pro"]
[7.343607, "o", "viders sign `\"<t>.<raw body>\"` with HMAC-SHA256 (`src/signature.ts`) and retry any\r\nnon-2xx response, so handlers must be idempotent and must answer 2xx only once the change is\r\nsaved. Answer 401 for a bad or stale signature, 404 for an unknown customer, 400 for a body\r\nthat is not JSON.\r\n\r\n## Audit trail\r\n\r\n`src/audit.ts` appends one JSON line per business event to `$AUDIT_LOG`\r\n(default `/var/tmp/audit/audit.ndjson`). The log shipper tails that file into Logline, where it\r\nis kept for 400 days and is searchable by everyone in Engineering, Support and Risk\r\n(about 140 people). Support use it to answer \"what happened to my account?\" tickets.\r\n"]
[7.34585, "o", "# Veriform webhooks (identity verification)\r\n\r\nVeriform runs our identity checks. When a check finishes it sends `check.completed`:\r\n\r\n```\r\nPOST /webhooks/veriform\r\nVeriform-Signature: t=1794823200,v1=<hex hmac>\r\nContent-Type: application/json\r\n```\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"id\": \"evt_8Qm2c7\",\r\n  \"type\": \"check.completed\",\r\n  \"created\": 1794823200,\r\n  \"data\": {\r\n    \"check\": {\r\n      \"id\": \"chk_31Hx0a\",\r\n      \"reference\": \"cus_1003\",\r\n      \"result\": \"rejected\",\r\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-11-16T10:00:00Z\",\r\n      \"reasons\": [\r\n        { \"code\": \"DOC_EXPIRED\", \"message\": \"Passport 533401187 expired on 2025-04-30\" }\r\n      ],\r\n      \"applicant\": {\r\n        \"full_name\": \"Daniel Okafor\",\r\n        \"date_of_birth\": \"1991-07-22\",\r\n        \"address\": { \"line1\": \"18 Grove Terrace\", \"city\": \"Leeds\", \"postcode\": \"LS6 2AB\", \"country\": \"GB\" }\r\n      },\r\n      \"document\": { \"type\": \"passport\", \"number\": \"533401187\", \"issuing_country\": \"GBR\", \"expiry\": \"2025-04-30\" },\r\n      \"liveness\": { \"score\": 0.94, \"selfie_url\": \"https://fil"]
[7.346185, "o", "es.veriform.example/s/chk_31Hx0a/selfie.jpg\" }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n- `reference` is the customer id we passed when we created the check.\r\n- `result`: `clear` (passed), `consider` (needs a person to look), `rejected` (failed).\r\n- `reasons` explains a `consider` or `rejected` result; empty for `clear`.\r\n  Codes: `DOC_EXPIRED`, `DOC_UNREADABLE`, `DOC_TAMPERED`, `NAME_MISMATCH`, `DOB_MISMATCH`,\r\n  `FACE_MISMATCH`, `LIVENESS_FAILED`, `WATCHLIST_HIT`.\r\n- Other event types (`check.started`, `check.reminder`) may be sent; nothing needs to happen\r\n  for them.\r\n- Veriform retries non-2xx responses with backoff for 24 hours and may deliver events out of\r\n  order.\r\n"]
